          "line": 320,
          "character": 66
        }
      },
      "title": "Stopping made-up IDs",
      "description": "**Q: How do you stop the model inventing account or ad unit IDs?**\n\n**A:** Entity grounding: real accounts, apps and ad units are loaded before the model runs and written into its prompt with *never invent IDs*. Tool inputs are then checked against them, and mediation groups get a strict check before and after approval.\n\n**If they push:** Default mode is soft, so other tools only log a warning on a bad id. The API then rejects it and the model gets an actionable error to fix."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/chat/graph/nodes/tool_executor.py",
      "line": 472,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 472,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 472,
          "character": 43
        }
      },
      "title": "Human in the loop",
      "description": "**Q: How does approval work?**\n\n**A:** Tools that write are detected by name and description. The tool executor validates the ids, then calls LangGraph's `interrupt()`, which pauses the run with its state saved in Postgres. The browser shows an editable form; on Allow, the run resumes with `Command(resume=...)`, re-validates any edits, and runs the tool.\n\n**If they push:** Own the gaps: the approve endpoint has no login check, resume doesn't check the run is yours, and a reload loses the stream id. Fixes: authenticate both, store the owner with the thread, keep the stream id server-side."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/server/routes/providers.ts",
      "line": 1226,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
