        }
      },
      "title": "Credentials",
      "description": "**Q: How does the agent use a user's Google account safely?**\n\n**A:** Tokens come from Google OAuth with offline access, are encrypted (JWE) at rest, and are never stored by the agent. Per request, the agent fetches a fresh token from an internal API endpoint protected by a shared secret, and passes it only to that user's tool process.\n\n**If they push:** Known weaknesses: the OAuth state isn't signed or stored (the waitlist's OAuth shows the fix), this endpoint's key check fails open if the secret is missing, and the agent caches tokens for an hour regardless of expiry."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/chat/tools/loader.py",
      "line": 295,
      "selection": {
