      },
      "title": "MCP",
      "description": "**Q: What is MCP and why use it here?**\n\n**A:** Model Context Protocol: a standard way to offer tools to a model. Each ad network gets its own MCP server, generated from that network's API description, run as a child process over stdio with the user's token in its environment. The agent stays generic; adding an endpoint means updating a spec, not writing a tool.\n\n**If they push:** Honest status: only AdMob and Ad Manager get credentials today; the other seven have tools but no login. The master server in `server.py` isn't used by the agent."
    },
    {
