      },
      "title": "Scaling",
      "description": "**Q: How would you scale it?**\n\n**A:** Graph state already lives in Postgres. The blockers are approvals and stream state in temp files and memory, and per-instance caches. I'd move those to Postgres or Redis, check thread ownership on resume, reuse one checkpointer connection pool instead of opening one per message, cache tokens by their real expiry, and let runs finish in the background if the browser disconnects."
    },
