      },
      "title": "Testing",
      "description": "**Q: How do you know it works?**\n\n**A:** Playwright end-to-end tests cover sign-in, streaming, entity resolution and the approval flow, with a test-only endpoint to seed approvals. There are 23 Python tests for the approval logic. LangSmith traces every run, Sentry catches errors, and run summaries track tokens and cost.\n\n**If they push:** Gaps to own: CI runs the leftover API copy's tests, the E2E workflow is manual, and the Python tests aren't in CI."
    },
    {
      "file": ".planning/codebase/CONCERNS.md",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "What would you change?",
      "description": "**Q: What would you improve?**\n\n**A:** 1. Authenticate approve and resume, and check run ownership. 2. Sign and store the OAuth state. 3. One internal-key header with a fail-closed check. 4. Pass credentials to the other seven networks, or drop them. 5. Wire up or delete the unused nodes and the backflow flags. 6. Delete `backend/api` and point CI at the live API. 7. Update the README.\n\n**If they push:** This file is the project's own list of concerns. Read its headings before an interview."
    },
